  "label": "PF Backlog 579",
  "title": "Eventing SSOT (Go): subscriber registry + dispatcher (cursor, at-least-once, dedupe, retry->DLQ)",
  "body": "## Problem / why\nNo persisted subscription registry and no cross-process dispatcher; delivery must be reliable.\n\n## Goal / value\nPersisted subscriber registry (single writer, store-registry entry) + a dispatcher that fans out with\nat-least-once delivery, event_id dedupe, and retry to the DLQ.\n\n## In scope\n- Subscription store {id, types[], filter, transport, target, auth_ref, enabled} registered in store-registry.json.\n- Dispatcher reading the stream via cursor; dedupe by event_id; retry/backoff -> core/dead_letter_queue.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Transport implementations (E5); alert policy (E6).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A registered subscription receives matching events exactly-once-effective; failures retry then DLQ.\n- Registry has one writer; no second event store.\n\n## Verification / test plan\n- Retry/DLQ test; dedupe test; concurrency test.",
